Q: Sheet component won&#39;t close after being opened even with open and onOpenChange props A: <p>That's a limitation by RadixUI - the headless UI behind shadcn. When the dialog (Sheet component is a dialog) is open, every element in page outside the <code>&lt;DialogContent /&gt;</code> (<code>&lt;SheetContent /&gt;</code>) is not accessible exept <code>&lt;DialogTrigger /&gt;</code> (<code>&lt;SheetTrigger /&gt;</code>).</p>
<p>For your information, You can use both <code>&lt;SheetTrigger /&gt;</code> with a controlled sheet.</p>
<pre><code>const Sidebar = () =&gt; {
    const [open, setOpen] = useState&lt;boolean&gt;(false);

    return (
        &lt;Sheet open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen}&gt;
            &lt;SheetTrigger className=&quot;p-0 flex border-0 cursor-pointer bg-transparent &quot;&gt;
                &lt;HamburgerMenu open={open} /&gt;
            &lt;/SheetTrigger&gt;
            &lt;SheetContent className=&quot;top-[3.5rem]&quot; side={&quot;left&quot;}&gt;
                &lt;SheetHeader&gt;
                    &lt;SheetTitle&gt;Are you absolutely sure?&lt;/SheetTitle&gt;
                    &lt;SheetDescription&gt;
                        This action cannot be undone. This will permanently
                        delete your account and remove your data from our
                        servers.
                    &lt;/SheetDescription&gt;
                &lt;/SheetHeader&gt;
            &lt;/SheetContent&gt;
        &lt;/Sheet&gt;
    );
};
</code></pre>
<p>This way, the <code>&lt;SheetTrigger /&gt;</code> will control opening and closing the dialog. and you still have access to the state to pass to your <code>&lt;HamburgerMenu /&gt;</code>. If possible, you can also utilise <code>[data-state=&quot;open&quot;]</code> attribute in <code>&lt;SheetTrigger /&gt;</code> to apply custom styles to the icon.</p>

